NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1036,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,2,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.5032,"rank":0.0402,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0001","role":"top","render":{"description":"A woman who can work magic and predict the future is said to have been born with a caul, which her parents did not burn but sold to sailors.","place":"Broek in Waterland","prov":"N.-H.","year":1898,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/8599","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ019021","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When he goes to look, the animal is nowhere to be found. An hour later he hears the same sound and this time the cat is there. The sound was an omen.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ031803","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It turns out she had a premonition of a later invention: the car, with its lights on.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0492"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"BIJLSMA001001","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Later the sound is heard again; then father has come home and thrown the spade into the boat.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0001","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"Only when the ship carrying the caul is wrecked is the woman freed of her gifts. She predicts that the doctor will not earn much from her, and dies a few months later.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"VODA_032_03","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A boy heard noise and saw a great fire at a farm, but suddenly the flames were gone. Later the farm really burned down. The boy had seen a voorspooksel or voorloop.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0491"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ075312","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"His mate, however, stays in the middle of the path and is then lifted up and set down further on.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ047907","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The clairvoyant also foresees that two black horses will refuse to pull the hearse. In the end a piebald horse will be harnessed to it. It turns out exactly that way.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ072402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Indeed, that evening a towboat arrived with its flag at half-mast.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ063401","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He says there is a light there, but it disappears at once. It was voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"WEV002003","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"follows the same route along which the dead boy is carried, and stops at the door through which he is brought inside.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ066503","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"You must not walk in the middle of the road, otherwise you will be flung aside by the funeral procession.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ044307","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Another man, who often foresaw that someone would die, warned that if the churchgoing man took his son to church again that Sunday, the son would die. The man paid no attention. That Sunday the boy died in an accident with a milk cart.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘woman’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0489. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"stack":["c1","c5"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1447,"rank":0.2897,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL003326","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"In the evening someone is jumped by a witch or werewolf.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210358","original":"Een ander verhaal uit de Nude: Iemand moest 's avonds de paarden naar de wei brengen. Toen gebeurde het eens, dat hem een \"teuverheks\" of een \"weerwolf\" op de rug sprong.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Tiel belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1089,"rank":0.159,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011312","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Near a canal people once heard hammering, but there was nothing to be seen. Two years later a wooden house was put up there.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17751","original":"It wie yn 1888 en 't gebeurde op it Blaufallaet. Doe wie dêr noch net it greate kanael, mar noch in gewoane feart. Myn mem wenne dêr. Sy is greatbrocht woarn by in âldomke fan my op it Blaufallaet. \nSy wie sawntsjin jier, doe stie se mei har omke op in joun bûtendoar. Oan 'e oare kant de feart gong it drok op in klunderjen. Mar der wie neat to sjen. \nMem sei: \"Dêr sil op in duer wol in hûs komme.\" Twa jier letter, yn 1890, woarde dêr in houten hûs delset. Greate Marten (Kalsbeek) kom der yn to wenjen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ021110","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Two men who were born with a caul saw funeral processions now and then.","place":"Haulerwijk","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20714","original":"Hjir wienen twa, dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen: Graanstra en âlde Merk. Sy seagen nou en dan lykstaesjes.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ036404","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A fortune teller makes predictions to two men about their future work and home and warns them to be careful of loose pieces of wood on the road to avoid accidents. Her predictions come true exactly.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22875","original":"Ik wie mei Bareld de Meer nei Snits ta to monsterjen. Mei de strikel yn 'e binnenbûse, om to ûngetiidzjen. Mar wy krigen beide gjin wurk. Bareld sei: \"Sille wy even nei Lytse Kjille ta op 'e Gerdyk? Dat wie in wiersizter.\nWy der hinne.\nKjille sei tsjin my: \"Binne jo troud?\"\n\"Ja\", sei 'k.\n\"Krij dan mar safolle kaerten\", sei se. Hja hie de kaerten út it laed helle fan 'e tafel. Hja gong by in stove op, sa kom se op 'e stoel. Sa lyts wie se.\n\"Om wurk út west?\" sei se. \"Ungetiidzje?\"\n\"Ja.\"\n\"En gjin wurk krige?\"\n\"Né\", sei 'k.\n\"Mar jo hà wurk\", sei se. \"Dêr geane jo moarn of oaremoarn hinne. Dêr fortsjinje jo fiifentwintich of seisentwintich goune. Der komt ek in nije wei by jimmes. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","2 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":2},"on_success":{"chime":2,"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.4888,"rank":0.5817,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ018116","role":"target","render":{"description":"A wit wief (white woman) haunts a certain haunted spot.","place":null,"prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20270"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ006221","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A woman is catching moles on the land with the eerie tree of the Bomklooster. Suddenly, some distance from her, two witte juffers (white maidens) walk across the land. When she goes over to look, they have vanished like snow before the sun.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16834","original":"In dochter fan Bouke Schievink wie us by 't maitiid oan 't mollebultstruijen op it lân fan Jan Binderts Kloosterman, fan 't Bomkleaster. Dat wie op dat stik lân mei de grouwe beam. Doe stapten dêr twa wite juffers oer 't lân, in moai ein fan har ôf. Sy gong der hinne om to sjen, mar doe wienen se samar fuort as snie foar de sinne. 't Gebeurde by de grouwe beam.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.18333,6.13333]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ079111","role":"helper","render":{"description":"On the Taekeland in Harkema a witte juffer (white lady) haunts.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28823","original":"Op it Taeke-Lân yn 'e Harkema, - dat leit by 't fuotbalfjild - spoeke in Wite juffer.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.20213,6.11183]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ110510","role":"helper","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a white lady haunts.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29563"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.21261,6.09209]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Kootstertille.","Find Sumar on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.18333,6.0],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Sumar"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2678,"rank":0.8234,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ063812","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Parken and in Rottefalle witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27145","original":"Hjir yn 'e Parken spoeken wite wiven en dat wie ek yn 'e Rottefalle it gefal.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING003002","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Girls haunt at night the place where they were murdered.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130952","original":"Ik arbeide op it sûkerijfebryk. Dêr fortsjinne ik twa goune yn de wike. Ik wier doe in jongfeint. Myn kameraten forgunden my dit ek noch. Op it Formanjepaed, hwer ik lâns moast nei it wurk, wierne troch in keardel twa famkes formoarde. Sont spûken dy dêr nachts altyd.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","original":"Witte wiven gingen altyd door 't bos van Jild Dyk. En so ferdwenen se weer. 't Waren twee witte frouljuu.\nDit gebeurde faak. Forskeidene hebben se sien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ061710","role":"member","render":{"description":"On the heath in Drenthe witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26899","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Broeksterwâld belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0901,"rank":0.7966,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ005402","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator's father was once going back from Sânbulten to Zwaagwesteinde at one o'clock at night. In the Zwagerbosch he suddenly saw five women standing there wearing pointed caps and long white skirts. There was not a breath of wind, yet the plumes of the caps waved to and fro. He was frightened to death and went to old Bearn's farm. When they went to look together, the women were gone.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16510","original":"Heit hat us in kear nei de Sânbulten to praten west. Om ien ûre yn 'e nacht gong er werom nei de Westerein ta. Op Sânbulten moest er oer 't spoar en sa kom er troch Sweagerbosk. 't Wie blêdstil en moai sacht waer. Der wie neat dat him forroerde.\nDoe seach heit dêr yn Sweagerbosk ynienen fiif froulju stean, allegear mei in puntmûtse op en lange wite rokken oan. Hoewol it blêdstil waer wie, waeiden de tûfen [fan] de puntmûtsen al mar hinne en wer. Heit wie deabinaud. Hy gong nei âlde Bearn op 't hiem en kloppe dêr op 'e achterdoar. Hy kloppe Bearn der út. Hy fortelde Bearn mei in triljend lûd hwat er sjoen hie. Doe gong Bearn mei him om nei dy froulju to sjen. Mar doe wie der net ien mear. Doe't heit yn 'e Westerein oankom, trille er noch.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ034801","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte juffers (white maidens) haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22700","original":"Us mem biwearde, to Aldegea spoeke it op in smel reedtsje by Jan Japiksma. Dêr wie in boskje mei in gracht der omhinne. Dêr spoeken wite juffers.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a crossroads near Jistrum it was haunted at night. One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12146","original":"Wite juffers\nTe Jistrum, oan 'e noardkant, dêr krúst de Spoekloane de wei dy't fan Jistrum nei de Grinzerstrjitwei rint. Op dat krúspunt doogde it lang net. Dêr gong wol ris in wite gestalte dwers oer de wei, flak foar de minsken lâns. Ik wit noch wol, dat ien fan Durk Jaringa's jonges-se wennen oan 'e grutte strjitwei- de jûnes nei 'De Lindeboom' yn Jistrum west hie - sa hiet de jachtweide fan Jan van der Schors. It hie der tige gesellich west, hy hie in slokje dronke en om in oere of tsien, alven sette er op hûs yn. Hy kaam dêr op dy fjouwersprong en dêr gong dy wite gestalte flak foar him lâns. Hy waard sa kjel, dat hy stode hals oer de kop wer nei Justrum ta en dêr fûn er andergeloks noch lju yn 'e herberch. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ZEEUW047","role":"card","render":{"description":"At night a white woman appears and disappears into a well. After the well is filled in, she no longer appears.","place":"Yerseke","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.D.v.O.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38973","original":"Witte Juffers\nOok te Ierseke verscheen de Witte Vrouw op een stuk grond tusschen Lepel- en Mosselstraat. Later heeft men uit de voorwerpen die daar gevonden zijn, kunnen nagaan dat dit opgehoogde terrein in de oudheid als kerkhof heeft gediend, en vermoedelijk ook een vluchtheuvel was.\nVele omwonenden hebben haar, in het holle van den nacht, gezien. Ze verdween dan altijd in een diepe welput. Na het dichten van de put, kwam de witte vrouw niet weer. Ze had rust gevonden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ063612","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Almelo they have witte wijven (white women) and a beautiful woman haunts the place. I heard that when I was buying horses there.","place":"Soesterberg","prov":"Utr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27090","original":"In Almelo hebben ze witte wiven. En daar spookt ook nog een mooie vrouw om. Ik heb het daar wel eens gehoord toen ik daar peerden kocht.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c6","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c6","word":"three","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"397f870baabf48b2","accepted_hashes":["0ad1ad7bd67f7aac3b220936a48e80a2ee2bf5d3df379ba14649883945d3e0d2","0ad522812dbb24dc5aa6ce18a07a6e8b0b5f2ec2008ba492bd5d7c7a250ccfcd","22f51904839817c0f4282c2ab4159998873ecc77e529ae82c00f336d070c0f78","279c1655197ca6892e03ea7d9a0f55f292b6b16356d1009c08fe1aa6cee10d16","511d417adf7d4a342f2ecc420690173887e2a1cc164756b37a580ad72e18189c"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0949,"rank":0.4963,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"member","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":null,"initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000115","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf leaps on people in the evening; as a helper with work; transformation into a werewolf by putting on a hidden coat, release after the coat is burned.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57969","original":"Weerwolven:\nMannen, die wat laat op de baan waren, werden, vooral in donkere, stormachtige nachten soms besprongen door de weerwolf. Dit spookdier met gloeiende ogen sprong hen op de rug, en klemde zich met de voorpoten om hun nek. Ze bleven zich als een zware last aan de verschrikte man klemmen totdat hij ergens een huis bereikte. In de Broekbeemd, tussen Onder-Eijndt en Zandberg, stond ergens een holle eiken knot of poesjt. Er was een man, die als weerwolf bekend werd. Hij had een aparte jas; als hij deze aantrok werd hij weerwolf. Na zijn nachtelijke tochten verborg hij deze jas in die holle “poesjt”. Zijn buurlui ontdekten dit, en staken de “poesjt” met de jas in brand. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"member","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","original":"Het weerwolfsvel verbrand\n\nBij de pachter van de boerderij bij het kasteel Geusselt onder Amby diende eens een scheper, een klein manneke, dat de naam had een weerwolf te zijn. 's Nachts was hij nooit in bed te vinden, maar 's morgens lag hij er weer in. De knechts van de hoeve hadden dat al dikwijls bemerkt.\nWijl dit zo opvallend was, werd zijn doen en laten gedurig bespied en zo bemerkte men dan ook dat hij, wanneer hij 's avonds uit zijn bed kroop, naar een weide ging, waar heel eenzaam een grote holle wilg stond. Daar verdween hij iedere keer in.\nOm het fijne van de zaak te achterhalen stuurde de pachter hem op zekere namiddag naar een dorp, dat meer dan drie uur van de hoeve lag, om daar koeien te kopen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Bathmen belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0416,"rank":0.3333,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ111718","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man out walking with a companion suspects that a man approaching them is a werewolf. When the werewolf comes closer, the man quickly throws him his red handkerchief. The werewolf then leaves the man alone. Because the two friends still want to know whether they were dealing with a real werewolf, they go to the man's house. When the man comes home, they shine a lantern in his face. The pieces of the red handkerchief are still hanging between his teeth. The man really is a werewolf.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29929","original":"Der wie in man, dy hie in gesin. Dy man wie in wjerwolf. By 't tsjuster wie er warber. Doe wie der in oaren ien dy wie mei syn maet der op út. Hja rounen togearre troch de Kûkhernster lânnen en doe kaem dy wjerwolf har tomjitte. De man, dy't mei syn maet wie fortocht de man fan dat gesin, dat dàt de wjerwolf wie, mar hy wist it net seker. Doe't dan dy wjerwolf oan harren ta wie, smiet er him gau syn reade bûsdoek ta en doe bleau de wjerwolf fan har ôf. Doe sei dy man tsjin syn maet: Litte wy ris nei dat en dat hûs ta gean - dat wie it hûs dêr't dy wjerwolf wenne. Hwant hy woe wite oft de bewenner fan dat hûs de wjerwolf wie.\nAllinne doarst hy der net hinne. Dêrom naem er syn kammeraet mei. 't Wie tusken Kûkherne en Burgumerheide. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST189","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058210","role":"door","render":{"description":"A werewolf is one of seven successive sons.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25993","original":"In wjerwolf is ien fan sawn opelkoar folgjende jonges, wurdt der altyd sein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.0592,"rank":0.8791,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ016705","role":"card","render":{"description":"A woman who sells butter always cheats her customers by never giving exactly the amount asked for. When she keeps haunting after her death, the minister asks her about her unfulfilled wish. The woman wants all her former customers to receive the butter they were owed, without having to pay for it. This is done and the woman finally finds rest.","place":"Eastermar","prov":"Fr.","year":1950,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20070","original":"Der mat in frou wenne ha op 'e Tike of sa. Dy forkocht wol bûter, mar sy hie de minsken noait it folle gewicht jown.\nSy kom to forstjerren, mar sy koe de rêst net fine. Sy kom hyltyd werom. Doe hellen de lju de dûmny derby en dy spruts har oan. Doe sei se hwat har bigearte wie. As de faem oan dy en dy minsken safolle bûter jaen woe, sûnder der sinten foar to freegjen, dan wie 't goed. De faem biloofde dat. It is gebeurd en it minske kom net wer.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ037108","role":"card","render":{"description":"A poor man made his wife promise never to part with the silver buckles on his shoes, but to keep them for their son. The man died and out of poverty the woman had to sell the buckles after all. But because of this the dead man could find no rest, and he appeared as a ghost to the woman and the children. The minister addressed the ghost and then saw to it that the buckles came back to the family. After that they never saw the apparition again.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23007","original":"De sulveren gaspen.\nDer wie in dokter yn Burgum en der wennen earme minsken yn Eastemar. Dy minsken hellen altyd de medesinen fan 'e dokter op foar de pasjinten yn Eastemar. Dêr koenen se in krom mei fortsjinje. De bern dienen dat meastal.\nMar doe kom dy frou hiel bot yn 'e earmoed to sitten, hwant har man stoar. Sy bleau allinne mei de bern sitten as in earme widdou.\nDe man hie skuon mei sulveren gaspen. Foar't er stoar hied er syn frou bilove litten dat dy sulveren gaspen, dy moesten der bliuwe foar ien fan syn jonges. Dy moest se letter op 'e skuon ha.\nMar, omt de frou sa yn earmoed forkearde, forkocht se op in dei de sulveren gaspen.\nDe bern gongen geregeld nei de dokter yn Burgum om medesinen op to heljen foar de lju fan Eastemar. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ081705","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmer had treated his parents rather badly. When he himself died, his inheritance was not divided as he had wanted. Every morning his household then saw him standing behind the house. They had the minister address the ghost. The farmer expressed his wish and the people carried it out. Since then the farmer has never come haunting again.","place":"De Tike","prov":"Fr.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29464","original":"Yn Sumar wenne in boer, dy hie syn folk (syn heit en mem) min bihandele. Dy boer kom to forstjerren. Mar de erfgenamten fordielden it erfskip net lyk as hy bigeard hie. Hy hie der by sein as se dat net dienen lyk as hy it ha woe, dat er dan wèr kom. En hy kòm wer. Hy koe de rêst net fine. Alle moarnen stie er op 'e achterhússtrjitte as se bigounen to fuorjen. Dêr waerden dy lju op 't lêst bang fan. Doe rôpen se de doomny der by. Dy doomny spruts him oan. Doe sei er tsjin dy doomny: sa en sa. Hja hienen syn bigearte net opfolge.\nDe doomny hat dat oerbrocht oan dy minsken en doe ha se it guod sa forparte lyk as hy dat wold hie. Doe ha se him net wer sjoen. Doe krige er rêst.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ081707","role":"card","render":{"description":"People who were not given grave clothes after their death came back to haunt later. Then they were addressed by the minister, and he made sure the matter was put right.","place":"De Tike","prov":"Fr.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29466","original":"Ik ha wolris heard fan guon, dy't de deaklean net meikrigen hienen, dat sokken har letter ek wer oppenearren. Dêr woarde dan ek in doomny by helle en dy makke dan dat de saek torjochte kom. Dy spruts de deade oan.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is a profession.","Begins with M. 8 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"397f870baabf48b2","accepted_hashes":["2812b56612c7005db093a1ad1658a943905633adcd7d40d098187edc2ae184b9","2db478a690098d2da1932c33ed123c0b0296fd4810d84e270bbf8dcc1e46d914","329168f9fafc792711ee744fb76ead6661cfd6a63965154e97cd62bb9894d6c5","5fd05604ec42b3a9ce212de19791e7f31f06b17293e060cb2a0b1a88cd8d22ce","86fbaf846e3fa35015011d9cc8246a0399aab1979cd3c3f150320fb6183df70a","c2898adb90f215ba7b75019e9efa4ee07b0e71b9a36a6cee032433959302a843","d1fe8ab78a11d99876080aa16257b86faea93d0fd4a2d02ad4d9158b39f6aafe","da978d017e5cb0cc3b0e8b5a08587290095f7522bb19826e18941d47a556c931","dabd5e5d3d5178126d23f961adf2107d9bde154ad061bf73c2b7b98045f99250"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.5242,"rank":1.2875,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ036919","role":"member","render":{"description":"A dead woman was buried in a shroud that was too long and keeps haunting after her death, calling 'Too long! Too long!'. After the minister has learned her problem from her, a piece of the shroud is torn off. Her ghost has never shown itself again.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22968","original":"Yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema wie in frou stoarn. Dy hie in bierkleed omkrige yn 'e kiste, dat hie to lang west.\nDoe koe dat minske de rêst net fine. En doe kom se elke joun by de famylje en dan rôp se: \"To lang! To lang!\"\nDoe ha dy lju doomny ophelle en dy hat har oansprutsen. Doe sei se, har bierkleed wie to lang, dêr moest in stik ôf.\nDoe is dêr in stik ôfskuord woarn en sûnt hat se har net wer fortoand.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ014310","role":"member","render":{"description":"A widower's second wife wore the first wife's clothes. But the children sometimes saw their first mother haunting in the wardrobe. The father did not believe it, but in the end sent for the minister. The spirit wanted clothes for her children to be made from her clothing, not for them to be worn by another woman.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19663","original":"Der leefde in man, dy forlear syn wiif. Hja hie in hiele protte klean fan har sels yn 'e kast. De man troude wer en sei tsjin it twadde wiif: \"Jo kinne dy klean wol drage.\"\nDoe seagen de bern har mem hyltyd wer kommen. Hja spoeke en roan nei de kast ta. Dat gebeurde wit hoe faek. Allinne de bern seagen it en sy fortelden it oan har heit. Mar dy woe 't net leauwe.\n\"Praetsjes\", sei er. Mar de bern bleauwen der by dat har mem nou en dan kom. Dat doe moest er 't op 't lêst ek wol leauwe. Doe helle hy de dûmny der by. Dy spruts it spoek oan.\n\"Hwat is jou bigearte?\" frege er.\n\"Dat de bern klean krije út de klean fan my\", sei se.\n\"Oaren matte se net oan ha.\"\nDat woarde dien en doe kom se net werom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ109806","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man plays at being a minister and mocks everything in his sermon. He never does it again, because at night the devil came to his bed.","place":"Feanwâlden","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38551","original":"Achter it café yn Feanwâlden stienen froeger banken. Dêr hâldde in kammeraet fan my in preek. Hy wie sabeare doomny. Hy spotte dat it hwat die en hie oeral de gek mei.\nDoe't er dy nachts op bêd lei, kaem de duvel by him. Doe die er it lekken oer de holle hinne, sa binaud waerd er.\nNoait hat er sokke dingen letter wer úthelle.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ013022","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happened that the dead came back when people did not keep the promises they had made during the dead person's life. The minister then had to come to ask the dead person what he wished.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19482","original":"It gebeurde wol, fortelde beppe, dat lju dy't stoarn wienen, weromkommen, as de minsken har net hâldden oan 'e bilofte dy't se sokken by har leven dien hienen. Dan moest der in dûmny by komme om sa'n forstoarne to freegjen hwat er winske.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Feanwâlden belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2143,"rank":0.7917,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer lives in a haunted farmhouse. When an old soldier comes begging, the farmer asks whether he will keep watch.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35028","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"half","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ015407","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she later goes to feed the pigs, the child's ghost keeps appearing. The child keeps putting its little hands on the pig trough.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ073804","role":"half","render":{"description":"Then Ruerd threatened to knock him down if he did not wait. The other then stopped. When Ruerd reached him, the other grabbed him several times and threw him over the trees. The next day they found him unconscious with all his ribs broken.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight the soldier sees six ghosts pass by; high-ranking officers who dig a hole by the haystack with their sabres. The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093904","role":"half","render":{"description":"He died in an accident with a horse and now his treasure lies there under the ground. The old man haunts the place and people are terrified. The old man keeps coming closer.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ082909","role":"half","render":{"description":"The man cannot bear it and fetches the minister. The minister says to the ghost: 'If you are of God, come to me; if you are of the devil, depart.' The ghost disappears and never comes back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
